From: Cubie A7S bringup <local>
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi-vin: export the OF modalias so udev auto-loads the driver

bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c registers a platform driver with a proper OF match
table but never exports it:

    static const struct of_device_id sunxi_vin_match[] = {
        {.compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-vin-media",},
        {},
    };
    static struct platform_driver vin_driver = {
        .driver = { .of_match_table = sunxi_vin_match, ... },
    };

Without MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, ...) the built modules carry no "of:" alias,
so udev has nothing to match the device modalias against and the driver is
never loaded automatically:

    $ modinfo vin_v4l2 | grep ^alias        # (no output)
    $ cat /sys/bus/platform/devices/vind@5800800/modalias
    of:NvindT(null)Callwinner,sunxi-vin-media

Observed on the running system (kernel 6.6.98-vendor-sun60iw2 #7): after
boot none of the VIN devices has a driver bound; only an explicit
`modprobe vin_v4l2` gets csi/mipi/isp/vind to probe.  A camera therefore
cannot work out of the box.

Add the missing MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sunxi_vin_match); the modules then
advertise

    alias: of:N*T*Callwinner,sunxi-vin-media

which matches the modalias above and makes udev load vin_io/vin_v4l2 (and
the sensor modules, which declare their own compatibles) on demand.

This is the same fix that was applied to the g2d driver
(patch/.../0011-g2d-module-autoload.patch).

Note: this is only half of the fix.  The top-level media device also needs
the three board supplies (vind_mclkpin/mcsipin/mipipin), otherwise probing
still fails with "error -1" before the OF alias can help -- see the
companion dts patch (0012-armbian-dts-cubie-a7s-mipi-csi-supplies.patch).

Baseline: Allwinner A733 SDK vendor kernel, bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c
  (2026-09-17 copy, md5 6e3e5f60766c432c7d39635836e177fc).
  Applies with `patch -p1` to the kernel tree used by the sun60iw2 vendor
  family.

---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c b/bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c
--- a/bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/vin/vin.c
@@ -2807,6 +2807,7 @@
 	{.compatible = "allwinner,sunxi-vin-media",},
 	{},
 };
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, sunxi_vin_match);
 
 static struct platform_driver vin_driver = {
 	.probe = vin_probe,
